<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Guard (Dominican Republic)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1924">1924</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Guardia Nacional Dominicana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Guard (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-panama">Guardia Nacional</a> Dominicana) was the constabulary created in 1917 by the US military government that occupied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a> from 1916 to 1924. Trained and led by US Marines, it replaced the old regional armies. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-trujillo">Rafael Trujillo</a> joined it in 1918 and rose through its ranks, using the force, later the National Army, to seize power in 1930.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-guard-dominican-republic.jpg" alt="National Guard (Dominican Republic)" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Croft · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_Dominican_Armed_Forces.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
